  {
   "id": "65fQGasECAAJ",
   "from": "Hugo Benítez",
   "author": "6909f45ba67d41fc",
   "date": "2017-07-20T01:18:23Z",
   "subject": "Principal Coordinate (Comparison of covariance matrices)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear geomorph community <br><br>I was wondering if the package have an option to compare more than 2 covariance matrices, like the use of Principal Coordinate analysis and if have integrated some distances to make this comparisons implemented at the package... I think it would be very useful indeed but I did not find anything related at the quick guide (maybe there are other article but one example is what Paula Gonzales with Benedikt Hallgrímsson did at 2011 J.Anatomy paper  <a href=\"http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/j.1469-7580.2010.01326.x/full\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/j.1469-7580.2010.01326.x/full&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486078472000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2OiCrdAzr1sP6prhU77Zzo\">http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/j.1469-7580.2010.01326.x/full</a> )<br><br>Thanks in advance<br><br>Best wishes<br>Hugo<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "Ciwwtgl2BwAJ",
   "from": "Adams, Dean [EEOBS]",
   "author": "4d71c6e24fb21497",
   "date": "2017-07-23T23:28:02Z",
   "subject": "Re: [geomorph-r-package] Principal Coordinate (Comparison of covariance matrices)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols\" dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<p>Hugo,</p>\r\n<p><br>\r\n</p>\r\n<p>No, at present this is not in geomorph. One could of course simply code this directly in R for the time being.</p>\r\n<p><br>\r\n</p>\r\n<p>Dean</p>\r\n<p><br>\r\n</p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div name=\"divtagdefaultwrapper\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Tahoma;font-size:13px\">\r\n<pre cols=\"72\">--  <br>Dr. Dean C. Adams<br>Professor<br>Department of Ecology, Evolution, and Organismal Biology<br>   Department of Statistics<br>Iowa State University<br><a href=\"http://www.public.iastate.edu/~dcadams/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.public.iastate.edu/~dcadams/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486078474000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1zCobiixXGvY_cTeZm2RGp\">www.public.iastate.edu/~dcadams/</a><br>phone: <a href=\"tel:(515)%20294-3834\" value=\"+15152943834\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">515-294-3834</a><br></pre>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<hr style=\"display:inline-block;width:98%\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" color=\"#000000\" style=\"font-size:11pt\"><b>From:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; on behalf of Hugo Benítez &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">hugobe...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Wednesday, July 19, 2017 8:18 PM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> geomorph R package<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [geomorph-r-package] Principal Coordinate (Comparison of covariance matrices)</font>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols\" dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear geomorph community <br>\r\n<br>\r\nI was wondering if the package have an option to compare more than 2 covariance matrices, like the use of Principal Coordinate analysis and if have integrated some distances to make this comparisons implemented at the package... I think it would be very useful\r\n indeed but I did not find anything related at the quick guide (maybe there are other article but one example is what Paula Gonzales with Benedikt Hallgrímsson did at 2011 J.Anatomy paper  <a href=\"http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/j.1469-7580.2010.01326.x/full\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/j.1469-7580.2010.01326.x/full&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486078474000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3yz96JTmHKvBvZsVFVYd9p\">http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/j.1469-7580.2010.01326.x/full</a>\r\n )<br>\r\n<br>\r\nThanks in advance<br>\r\n<br>\r\nBest wishes<br>\r\nHugo<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<p></p></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
